          <h2 class="font-bold text-white text-lg">Vehicle Data Accuracy</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="px-6 py-5 prose-dark">
          <p class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">VIN decoding results and vehicle specifications displayed on Car Alpha are sourced from the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA) Vehicle Product Information Catalog (VPIC) database. Recall data is sourced from the NHTSA Office of Defects Investigation.</p>
          <p class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">While NHTSA data is the authoritative federal source for vehicle information, it has known limitations:</p>
          <ul class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-2 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Some fields may be incomplete, especially for older vehicles or specialty manufacturers</li>
            <li>Data is provided as reported by vehicle manufacturers to NHTSA and may contain errors at the source</li>
            <li>Recall data reflects federally mandated safety recalls and may not include all manufacturer service campaigns or technical service bulletins</li>
            <li>Vehicle specifications may not account for dealer-installed options or aftermarket modifications</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-silver-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3"><strong>Always verify vehicle information with the manufacturer, dealer, or a qualified mechanic before making any decision based on data from this site.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-card metallic-border rounded-2xl overflow-hidden carbon-panel">
